let __v_601 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"daffodil\",\"daffodils\",\"hyacinth\",\"hyacinths\",\"crocus\",\"snowdrop\",\"snowdrops\",\"allium\",\"alliums\",\"spring bulbs\"]},\"Spring bulbs go in from September to November while the soil is still warm: three times the bulb's own height deep, 10cm apart for daffodils and 8cm for crocuses, pointy end up. They need a cold spell to flower, so a mild autumn is fine. Leave the leaves on for six weeks after flowering and they come back every year.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sweet pea\",\"sweet peas\"]},\"Sow sweet peas in October for the strongest plants, or February to March under cover, 2cm deep in deep pots so the root runs straight down. Pinch out the growing tip after two pairs of leaves, harden them off, and plant out in April. Keep picking, because once they set seed they stop flowering.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"strawberry\",\"strawberries\",\"strawberry plants\"]},\"Plant strawberries in late summer, August to September, for a full crop the next June - a spring planting gives you a handful the same year and nothing much the next. 45cm apart with the crown level with the soil and the roots spread, straw under the fruit, and replace the plants every three years, when the crop shrinks and virus builds up.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"grass seed\",\"lawn seed\",\"grass\"]},\"Sow grass seed in September, or early April if you missed it: warm damp soil, weeds not yet up, and enough time to root before winter. Scatter 35g to the square metre, rake it in lightly, and keep it damp for a fortnight with a light sprinkle morning and evening rather than a soak.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tomato\",\"tomatoes\",\"tomato plants\"]},\"Sow tomatoes indoors in March or April and plant them out in early June, once nights stay above 10C: 45cm apart, or one to a grow bag, burying the stem up to its first leaves. Harden them off over a week first - a cold night sets a tomato back a month.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tree\",\"trees\",\"fruit tree\",\"bare root\",\"bare-root\",\"shrub\",\"shrubs\",\"hedge\",\"hedges\",\"clematis\",\"climber\",\"climbers\",\"wisteria\"]},\"Bare-root trees and shrubs go in from November to March while they are dormant, and potted ones any time the ground is not frozen or waterlogged. Dig a square hole twice the width of the roots, keep the soil mark on the stem at the same level, firm it in well and water it through its first summer. Autumn planting beats spring: the roots work all winter.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rose\",\"roses\",\"bare root rose\",\"climbing rose\",\"shrub rose\"]},\"Plant bare-root roses from November to March, while they are dormant, or potted ones any month the ground is not frozen: a hole wide enough to spread the roots, the graft union an inch below soil level, firmed in hard. They want sun and rich soil, and a feed in March and again in July is what keeps them flowering.\"]}]}")?;
