let __v_980 = Value::from("Water deeply and less often, in the evening or early morning: a good soak twice a week in a dry spell beats a light sprinkle every day, because it reaches the roots instead of wetting the surface. Aim at the soil, not the leaves. Established shrubs, borders and perennials need nothing until the soil is dry a spade's depth down, while anything newly planted and anything in a pot is the exception and wants water every day or two in heat.");
